sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Murray (1926a, 1926b), Zamir (1976) & Sherman (1981) minimum-work vascular cube law & arterial branching angles — MorphoEval overall 48.2/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 1 (v1 baseline) evaluation of `1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py` (51.4/100). The v1 script implements Murray's (1926a) Poiseuille viscous power + metabolic blood-volume cost functional P(r) = 8*eta*L*Q^2/(pi*r^4) + b*pi*r^2*L, stationarity radius r*, symmetric cube law r_0^3 = 2*r_1^3 (r_1/r_0 = 2^(-1/3)), and symmetric optimal branching angle (theta_1 + theta_2 = 74.93 deg), but omits asymmetric daughter bifurcations (alpha = r_2/r_1 < 1), omits alternative optimality ablations (Da Vinci area-preserving gamma=2, Zamir 90 deg surface-area minimization, Steiner 120 deg length minimization), neither loads nor verifies `datasets/vascular_cube_law_branching/vascular_cube_law_branching_reference.json`, and performs zero biological specimen segmentation on `datasets/vascular_cube_law_branching/retinal_vasculature_specimen.jpg`. Overall 48.2/100 (faithfulness 41.9, reproducibility 63.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 62, Morphological realism / specimen match 22, Parameter expressivity 42, Morphometric validation 48, Source and data traceability 58, Code-to-model traceability 62, Reproducibility package 68. Output judged: docs/media/vascular_cube_law_branching_comparison.png: rendered output of 1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py at 8871db0, image/png, 153263 B, 1960×644 px, artifact_sha256 a251584c0520dfda3240e751daff491369bf2f1d5799dad6103cc3cd1423c455 (sha256 a251584c0520dfda3240e751daff491369bf2f1d5799dad6103cc3cd1423c455), spec_fingerprint 28bf2bb7d9ebb4ea9c5721cc29a875189747c8344d5828934425a1601bbeb74e. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 28bf2bb7d9ebb4ea9c5721cc29a875189747c8344d5828934425a1601bbeb74e; artifact_sha256: a251584c0520dfda3240e751daff491369bf2f1d5799dad6103cc3cd1423c455; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/vascular_cube_law_branching/retinal_vasculature_specimen.jpg=bc548d4150e070a5..., datasets/vascular_cube_law_branching/vascular_cube_law_branching_reference.json=450775cc5fc7ee81...}." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Expand `--self-test`, CLI parameter flags (`--alpha`, `--gamma`, `--eta`, `--b`, `--generations`, `--seed`), and `measure_morphoeval()` to report >= 8 quantitative metrics with reference values, dispersion (RMSE, CV, std), and negative-control deltas.",
            "remediation needed: Implement competing optimality negative controls and ablations: Da Vinci area-preserving branching (gamma = 2.0, r_0^2 = r_1^2 + r_2^2), Zamir (1976) lumen-surface-minimizing branching (theta_1 + theta_2 = 90 deg), and Steiner length-minimizing branching (theta_1 + theta_2 = 120 deg), quantifying total hydraulic + metabolic power penalty (% excess work) relative to Murray's gamma = 3.0 optimum.",
            "remediation needed: Implement full asymmetric arterial bifurcation laws cos(theta_1), cos(theta_2), and cos(theta_1 + theta_2) across alpha = r_2/r_1 in [0.1, 1.0] (Murray 1926b Eqs. 3-6) and verify scale-invariant wall shear stress tau_w = 4*eta*Q/(pi*r^3) = sqrt(eta*b) across all 7 Sherman (1981) arteriole generations.",
            "remediation needed: Load and SHA-256-verify `datasets/vascular_cube_law_branching/vascular_cube_law_branching_reference.json` and `retinal_vasculature_specimen.jpg` at runtime, segment the human retinal vasculature fundus panels (Frangi/multi-scale matched-filter vessel enhancement, medial-axis skeletonization, distance-transform vessel caliber estimation, and Y-junction angle/radius ratio extraction), and compare against empirical human retinal junctions J01-J08 (RMSE, Pearson r, CV)." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.482"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (MorphoEval Loop 052 Assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .
}

